# Product docs (not in every chat)

Requirements and roadmap stay in **`docs/`** (readable on GitHub, shareable outside Cursor). Do **not** duplicate full PRD/plan into rules unless you intentionally want huge always-on context.

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `docs/prd.md` | Functional requirements, product scope |
| `docs/plan.md` | Phases, roadmap, current focus |

**Easiest use:** `@docs/prd.md` and/or `@docs/plan.md` in chat when the task touches product behavior, priorities, or “what should this feature do?”

If you are editing `lib/` and those files are not in context yet, open or attach them before implementing behavior changes.
